		(property "Part Origin" "Exact-MPN migration research from historical P-00015 context only; no inherited verification, project edits or substitute approval. Symbol from KiCad Device:C. Reuses unchanged managed verified:C_1210_3225Metric. Provisional geometric fit only, per latest request clarification; not assembly approval or placement-tolerance analysis. Nonpolar terminals map to pads 1 and 2. Catalog pads at x +/-1.475 mm are 1.15 x 2.70 mm. At centered placement, minimum end-terminal strips at body-length extremes occupy x 1.150..1.450 and 1.450..1.750 mm (opposite terminal mirrored), within the positive pad span 0.900..2.050 mm; transverse pad width accommodates maximum 2.70 mm body width. Courtyard +/-2.30 x +/-1.60 mm surrounds maximum body +/-1.75 x +/-1.35 mm. Retained gap 1.80 mm and width 2.70 mm differ from Murata p27 recommended gap 2.0..2.4 mm and width 1.8..2.3 mm; pad length 1.15 mm is within 1.0..1.2 mm. This is NOT a manufacturer-recommended land pattern. Murata p27 requires actual PCB evaluation; p16 warns excessive solder can stress/crack MLCCs. Human exact-part review must assess this assembly deviation and solder amount before verification. Reviewed copper/mask/paste and courtyard retained unchanged; no new stencil specification or waiver. Unchanged reviewed generic STEP measured x +/-1.60, y +/-1.25, z 0..2.50 mm, matching nominal body envelope only. It does not represent tolerance extremes or exact manufacturer termination construction. Exact-part maximum height is 2.70 mm; use this, plus assembly allowances, for clearance rather than the nominal model. Generic model reuse does not qualify this MPN."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(hide yes)
